<title>USA: EuroMed says Nasdaq to delist firms shares.</title>
<headline>EuroMed says Nasdaq to delist firms shares.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>EuroMed Inc said on Friday the Nasdaq decided to delist the shares of the company's common stock because of alleged violations by the company of certain NASD markteplace rules.</p>
<p>The company said in a written release that it plans to request a review of the decision and is in the process of applying to the over-the-counter electronic bulletin board.</p>
<p>Company officials were not available for comment.</p>
<p>EuroMed also said it is restructuring its board of directors.</p>
</text>
